nodecode-teammates is a rewrite of 100yenadmin's 100yenadmin/hermes-teammates:

  https://github.com/100yenadmin/hermes-teammates
  commit bdfe621a8e5334f41002344da5bdfe49af01b693
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Electric Sheep (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the roster of named teammates and the tools over it -- assign a
goal, check a run and its answer, wait for runs to come to rest, message one
(a steer while it runs, its next turn when it is at rest), stop it, and list
the roster with this conversation's runs -- plus the /teammates command, the
per-teammate description the agent picks by, the instructions a run works
under, and an optional provider and model pin. The plugin's SQLite ledger and
its own subagent lifecycle calls are replaced by Nodecode's own durable
sessions: a run is an ordinary session under the session that assigned it, so
its transcript carries its earlier work and the run ids are kept in the
assigning session's per-session state.

Left out: the Hermes Kanban lane and its review handoff (there is no board in
the same sense here), the per-teammate toolset narrowing, the completion
notice that Hermes reserved without sending, and the character-budgeted
follow-up digest -- a follow-up in this rewrite goes to the run's own
session, which already holds everything it did.

